<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador public foreign debt at $12.49 bln in May.</title>
<headline>Ecuador public foreign debt at $12.49 bln in May.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's public foreign debt in May rose 0.49 percent from April and stood at $12.49 billion, a Central Bank report said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The public foreign debt in May 1996 was $12.41 billion.</p>
<p>Private foreign debt stood at $2.15 billion in May 1997.</p>
<p>Total foreign debt rose to $14.65 billion in May, up from $14.59 billion in April.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429 x114</p>
